WEBVTT

00:03.730 --> 00:08.360
Oh my. I'm surprised to 
see someone else here.

00:09.850 --> 00:11.280
You by yourself?

00:11.280 --> 00:12.210
Yes.

00:12.600 --> 00:16.600
The Tarasque Swamp isn't a 
place for a normal person...

00:16.600 --> 00:19.080
Particularly not alone.

00:19.770 --> 00:24.340
You seem to be implying you're not normal.

00:24.770 --> 00:28.990
I simply possess a magic 
item that nullifies poison,

00:28.990 --> 00:31.510
and holy water that drives Tarasques away,

00:31.510 --> 00:34.920
as well as an accurate map.

00:35.860 --> 00:38.440
I'm after the Dragonblood flowers.

00:38.930 --> 00:41.430
You don't mind if I take some, do you?

00:41.960 --> 00:42.930
Help yourself.

00:49.550 --> 00:53.260
<i>Yeah, I'm the one who's sure not normal.</i>

02:30.370 --> 02:35.550
<b>A Strange Man
and a Strange Job</b>

02:34.910 --> 02:36.580
Is that all you need?

02:37.320 --> 02:38.500
Yes.

02:38.820 --> 02:44.130
My mistress wants the 
Dragonblood flower itself.

02:44.540 --> 02:47.740
The medicine you make from 
these will last a while,

02:47.740 --> 02:50.320
but the flowers themselves won't 
if they're plucked, right?

02:50.680 --> 02:51.680
Yes.

02:52.320 --> 02:56.570
I'm sorry for prying, but 
is your mistress badly ill?

02:57.030 --> 02:58.960
Yes, I suppose so.

02:58.960 --> 03:01.750
I'd like to stay by their side,
taking care of them.

03:02.450 --> 03:04.440
I know this doesn't help, but...

03:05.060 --> 03:07.150
I hope they get better soon.

03:07.840 --> 03:09.740
Thank you.

03:10.130 --> 03:15.280
I and my mistress were fortunate I 
was able to make your acquaintance.

03:16.930 --> 03:18.640
I was just looking for someone

03:18.640 --> 03:23.090
who could bring us Dragonblood 
flowers at regular intervals.

03:23.580 --> 03:27.000
It's silly to be asking this now, 
but you're an adventurer, right?

03:27.420 --> 03:30.760
I'm Rentt Vivie. A 
Bronze-class adventurer...

03:31.510 --> 03:33.820
Bronze-class?

03:33.820 --> 03:35.130
Change your mind?

03:35.730 --> 03:37.020
Not at all.

03:37.020 --> 03:39.640
I'm certain you're strong enough.

03:39.980 --> 03:43.780
If the pay and conditions are to your liking,

03:43.780 --> 03:47.160
I would appreciate it if you would accept.

03:48.060 --> 03:49.520
Alright.

03:49.520 --> 03:52.130
We'll make the arrangements 
after our return, then.

03:52.130 --> 03:54.700
Oh, I haven't introduced myself.

03:55.440 --> 03:57.610
I'm Isaac Hart.

03:58.090 --> 04:00.040
As for my mistress...

04:00.590 --> 04:03.730
I'll introduce you after the 
arrangements are finalized.

04:08.560 --> 04:11.890
I didn't realize you were so strong.

04:11.890 --> 04:15.730
Not many people come back 
from that swamp unharmed.

04:16.090 --> 04:20.770
Actually, this mask is just 
a way to hide my identity.

04:21.490 --> 04:24.370
I'm actually a Mythril-class adventurer.

04:26.830 --> 04:28.870
Make sure you hire me next time!

04:28.870 --> 04:30.610
I'll give you a discount!

04:33.490 --> 04:34.740
Rentt!

04:35.500 --> 04:39.660
I'd like to return this magic bag and 
hire someone to butcher a monster.

04:39.660 --> 04:41.140
Butcher...?

04:41.510 --> 04:43.630
Did you defeat one?

04:49.650 --> 04:51.350
There's a lot.

04:51.350 --> 04:52.700
Okay.

04:52.700 --> 04:55.770
I'll show you to the Butcher's, then.

04:57.010 --> 04:59.180
<i>A monster doesn't just drop magic stones.</i>

04:59.180 --> 05:01.730
<i>Their bodies can be butchered to 
provide many different materials.</i>

05:02.110 --> 05:05.470
<i>I learned how to do the basics myself when I 
was learning to be a hunter in the village,</i>

05:05.470 --> 05:10.590
<i>but for things I can't handle, I pay 
the money to hire a specialist.</i>

05:13.990 --> 05:15.550
Dario!

05:16.930 --> 05:18.150
Hey!

05:18.150 --> 05:19.310
What's up?

05:19.700 --> 05:23.890
Rentt here has brought 
something unusual for us.

05:25.020 --> 05:26.710
A Tarasque!

05:27.100 --> 05:28.360
A Tarasque?

05:31.750 --> 05:33.850
Okay, bring it out!

05:33.850 --> 05:36.290
Will Edel be okay?

05:36.290 --> 05:38.560
Edel's resistant to poison.

05:48.900 --> 05:50.870
It's big.

05:51.390 --> 05:54.080
And in good shape, too.

05:54.080 --> 05:56.160
Not a single wound on the shell.

05:56.160 --> 05:57.570
That's rare.

05:57.570 --> 05:59.080
Is it?

05:59.080 --> 06:00.140
Yes.

06:00.140 --> 06:02.360
The normal way to fight 
one of these is to attack

06:02.360 --> 06:04.880
from outside the range of 
its poison to weaken it.

06:04.880 --> 06:07.780
So the shell always gets damaged.

06:08.100 --> 06:09.720
I see.

06:09.720 --> 06:13.370
You killed it in basically 
a single hit, right?

06:13.370 --> 06:15.590
A <i>single</i> hit?

06:15.590 --> 06:18.750
I just didn't have time 
to land multiple hits.

06:18.750 --> 06:20.820
Don't be so humble!

06:20.820 --> 06:24.210
I haven't seen a Tarasque 
of this quality in ages.

06:24.600 --> 06:26.590
Will it be worth a lot?

06:26.590 --> 06:27.650
Of course.

06:28.220 --> 06:30.070
Can I ask you to handle it?

06:30.070 --> 06:31.230
Yes.

06:31.230 --> 06:32.860
Look forward to it.

06:33.460 --> 06:34.630
Thanks.

06:38.970 --> 06:42.150
I guess I'll go to the orphanage tomorrow.

06:42.150 --> 06:44.290
Thanks for staying out so late with me.

06:44.290 --> 06:45.420
Not at all.

06:45.420 --> 06:50.170
Anyway, Rentt, you've gotten 
a lot stronger, haven't you?

06:50.810 --> 06:52.170
Have I?

06:52.170 --> 06:55.460
You defeated that huge 
Tarasque all by yourself!

06:55.460 --> 06:57.370
You're at the high end of Bronze...

06:57.370 --> 07:00.570
No, you could easily be Silver!

07:00.570 --> 07:02.660
You should remember that.

07:10.200 --> 07:12.910
<i>I do feel stronger, but...</i>

07:13.900 --> 07:19.740
<i>But saying that I, myself, have 
gotten stronger feels weird.</i>

07:21.100 --> 07:23.740
<i>Isaac doesn't seem to be an adventurer,</i>

07:23.740 --> 07:28.170
<i>but he's probably got the strength of a 
Silver-class, or probably close to Gold!</i>

07:28.820 --> 07:32.830
<i>I just took advantage of my undead body.</i>

07:34.530 --> 07:40.800
<i>This strength is something I got 
just by becoming a monster.</i>

07:41.970 --> 07:44.010
<i>Of course, I want to go back to being human.</i>

07:44.620 --> 07:50.260
<i>But without this power, I'll go 
back to who I was then, right?</i>

07:51.270 --> 07:54.020
<i>10 years... 10 years!</i>

07:54.750 --> 07:57.220
<i>With no talent, no getting better...</i>

07:57.220 --> 08:00.040
<i>Where putting in effort each 
day was all I could do...</i>

08:01.670 --> 08:05.950
<i>Could I go back to that, and 
still try to become Mythril?</i>

08:17.330 --> 08:20.310
This is fine. I've got just the thing.

08:22.540 --> 08:24.050
Perfectly done.

08:24.710 --> 08:26.360
What's perfectly done?

08:27.830 --> 08:29.220
The job.

08:29.220 --> 08:30.870
Already?!

08:34.380 --> 08:35.830
This is it...

08:35.830 --> 08:37.370
I've never seen it before.

08:37.690 --> 08:39.310
It's beautiful!

08:39.310 --> 08:41.140
This is wonderful.

08:41.140 --> 08:45.150
It's rare to see one that's 
been prepared so well.

08:45.150 --> 08:46.570
Is it?

08:46.570 --> 08:50.580
The only adventurers who go to the Tarasque 
swamp are of fairly high rank, right?

08:51.010 --> 08:53.870
They should all know how 
to properly prepare herbs.

08:54.160 --> 08:56.160
Well, just because of the 
kind of place it is,

08:56.160 --> 08:58.940
there's not a lot of time 
to do things properly.

08:58.940 --> 09:02.050
Sometimes you can get attacked 
by a Tarasque on your way out.

09:02.050 --> 09:05.880
You must be a powerful adventurer.

09:05.880 --> 09:08.570
I'm Umberto, the healer.

09:08.800 --> 09:09.780
And this is...

09:09.780 --> 09:11.790
Norman. An herbalist.

09:11.790 --> 09:14.680
Wow, with something of this quality

09:14.680 --> 09:17.570
I can make a medicine to treat 
Malaccumula really quickly.

09:17.570 --> 09:18.590
Really?

09:18.590 --> 09:23.110
Yes. If there's any left over, can I use it?

09:23.110 --> 09:24.770
There are people who need it.

09:24.770 --> 09:26.490
Of course. I don't mind.

09:26.990 --> 09:28.570
Do you want more?

09:29.950 --> 09:31.470
Of course...

09:31.470 --> 09:34.290
I'd be lying if I said I didn't.

09:35.200 --> 09:36.670
Is this enough?

09:37.110 --> 09:40.480
No need to pay me. Just put it to good use.

09:41.790 --> 09:45.060
You sure? This would be 
worth a lot of money.

09:45.470 --> 09:47.600
It's nice to just help 
people, once in a while.

09:47.970 --> 09:50.600
Thank you. This is wonderful.

09:50.910 --> 09:54.820
I'll be able to save so 
many lives with these...

09:54.820 --> 09:56.870
We can't repay you right now,

09:56.870 --> 09:59.730
but if you need something 
in the future, tell us.

09:59.730 --> 10:00.620
I will.

10:10.190 --> 10:11.370
And there we go.

10:12.690 --> 10:15.170
This completes the job.

10:15.170 --> 10:16.140
Thanks.

10:17.250 --> 10:18.400
Here you go.

10:18.400 --> 10:19.670
Thank you.

10:19.670 --> 10:20.820
No...

10:20.820 --> 10:24.330
I'm the one who has to thank you.

10:24.330 --> 10:26.540
I can't thank you enough!

10:27.110 --> 10:32.860
I was going to become an adventurer and 
get it myself if nobody took the job...

10:32.860 --> 10:34.820
But I don't think that would've worked.

10:34.820 --> 10:37.520
You no longer want to be an adventurer?

10:39.600 --> 10:41.900
I actually want to be one even more.

10:42.520 --> 10:43.780
Rentt...

10:43.780 --> 10:46.340
I want to be an adventurer like you!

10:47.750 --> 10:51.130
One who can help people!

10:51.480 --> 10:52.450
Like me?

10:52.750 --> 10:54.400
Thank you so much!

10:54.400 --> 10:57.950
I can't do anything to thank you, but if...

10:59.970 --> 11:03.480
There's nothing I can do 
to help you, is there?

11:03.480 --> 11:05.070
That's not true.

11:05.940 --> 11:09.540
There are times when I need help, too.

11:09.990 --> 11:12.310
When that happens, I'll come to you.

11:13.920 --> 11:16.720
Great! You'd better!

11:16.720 --> 11:17.490
Sure.

11:19.460 --> 11:20.990
Was everything okay?

11:22.470 --> 11:27.510
Alize, you said there were sometimes 
small monsters in the basement, right?

11:27.510 --> 11:29.750
Yes. That's right.

11:29.750 --> 11:32.610
Edel's old gang will protect you.

11:32.610 --> 11:35.490
Gang... Of puchi suri?

11:36.370 --> 11:38.090
That's great!

11:38.090 --> 11:39.730
Thank you, Edel!

11:41.580 --> 11:43.060
That's so great...

11:43.060 --> 11:47.880
I wonder if I'll be able to tame monsters 
like this when I become an adventurer.

11:48.960 --> 11:53.520
Anyway, if you want to be an adventurer, 
you should start training early.

11:53.520 --> 11:54.790
Training?

11:54.790 --> 11:56.830
The guild holds classes.

11:57.240 --> 12:00.140
And I can train you too, when I have time.

12:00.140 --> 12:01.490
Really?

12:01.490 --> 12:06.190
If you have mana, you should 
learn to use magic, too.

12:06.190 --> 12:09.250
But I don't have money...

12:09.710 --> 12:11.250
It's expensive to train with a sword,

12:11.650 --> 12:16.090
but training to learn magic 
costs even more, right?

12:16.500 --> 12:19.070
I've got a friend who's not 
doing anything with her time.

12:19.070 --> 12:20.590
Don't worry about it.

12:20.590 --> 12:22.050
That won't do!

12:22.580 --> 12:24.870
I can't count on you for that much.

12:24.870 --> 12:27.640
Then I'll lend you the 
money, with no interest.

12:28.790 --> 12:33.060
When you become an adventurer and 
start earning money, pay me back.

12:36.390 --> 12:38.360
I'll pay it back with interest.

12:38.870 --> 12:39.970
Got it.

12:40.580 --> 12:43.040
We have a deal, then.

12:46.620 --> 12:49.090
I look forward to doing 
business with you, Rentt!

12:51.080 --> 12:54.840
I don't mind teaching her.

12:54.840 --> 12:58.220
There are indeed times when 
I'm "not doing anything".

13:00.150 --> 13:02.310
As you say.

13:02.310 --> 13:06.440
Sorry... I meant when you're free.

13:06.440 --> 13:09.410
You should be careful with your words.

13:09.410 --> 13:13.190
You don't understand how young girls feel.

13:15.850 --> 13:18.150
Thanks for the warning.

13:18.150 --> 13:22.650
I have very few interactions 
with young girls, though.

13:22.650 --> 13:25.130
That's not true.

13:25.860 --> 13:27.790
There's a young girl you know quite well.

13:29.450 --> 13:30.420
See?

13:32.190 --> 13:32.990
Where?

13:34.240 --> 13:40.020
I just remembered about this extremely 
powerful spell I just developed...

13:40.020 --> 13:41.680
L-Lorraine?

13:42.560 --> 13:47.170
Let's see just how much that 
undead body of yours can take!

13:47.170 --> 13:49.250
Wait! You're young!

13:49.250 --> 13:51.150
You're very young, Lorraine!

13:51.630 --> 13:54.000
Your skin is as fair as driven snow...

13:54.000 --> 13:57.970
And your statuesque figure...

13:58.770 --> 14:02.160
Even the water fairies created 
by the goddess of beauty

14:02.160 --> 14:06.130
as the physical manifestation of 
her virtue would bow their heads

14:06.130 --> 14:08.200
at the sight of your gorgeous face!

14:08.200 --> 14:13.630
You are the very picture of a young 
girl in every way, Lorraine!

14:14.610 --> 14:20.170
Where the hell did you 
learn to talk like that?

14:20.170 --> 14:24.260
Don't tell me you say that 
to every girl you meet.

14:24.260 --> 14:25.890
Of course I don't!

14:26.540 --> 14:27.800
I mean...

14:28.280 --> 14:30.600
I just said what I was thinking.

14:33.960 --> 14:36.040
You'd like a little more to eat, right?

14:36.040 --> 14:36.930
Uh...

14:36.930 --> 14:39.140
I'll bring you something.

14:40.130 --> 14:44.600
I split the pots between the one 
with blood and the one without.

14:52.550 --> 14:54.850
I think that got to me a little...

15:05.000 --> 15:08.910
<i>Why am I the only one working 
when I'm the master?</i>

15:10.070 --> 15:10.880
Rentt!

15:11.660 --> 15:12.760
Morning!

15:12.760 --> 15:14.460
Can we talk?

15:14.840 --> 15:15.910
This way.

15:19.320 --> 15:21.060
What's this about?

15:21.060 --> 15:26.540
Um, Rentt, did you know anyone 
in the Latour household?

15:26.540 --> 15:28.050
The Latour household?

15:28.050 --> 15:29.610
You don't?

15:30.090 --> 15:31.790
I've never heard the name.

15:32.850 --> 15:37.140
There's actually a job 
requesting you specifically.

15:39.070 --> 15:41.630
Oh, the one from Isaac?

15:41.630 --> 15:44.490
So you do know them?

15:45.050 --> 15:46.120
No...

15:48.470 --> 15:53.530
I just know a man who I assume is a 
servant of this Latour Household.

15:54.710 --> 15:57.310
Is the family that famous?

15:57.310 --> 16:01.370
I'd like to think I know most of 
what there is to know about Maalt.

16:01.370 --> 16:03.760
I know little about them, myself.

16:04.080 --> 16:10.870
They're not nobles, but they're a very old 
house with a lot of influence over Maalt.

16:11.250 --> 16:16.700
Someone of my lowly station 
wouldn't be told any more.

16:16.700 --> 16:19.460
So they're very secretive.

16:19.460 --> 16:24.290
Each generation's guild master 
is told to be very careful

16:24.290 --> 16:26.920
not to offend the Latour household.

16:27.660 --> 16:30.580
Rentt, if you're going to live here in Maalt,

16:30.580 --> 16:33.720
you absolutely cannot refuse 
a request from the Latours.

16:34.400 --> 16:36.260
I have no intention of refusing.

16:36.260 --> 16:39.290
But... is it okay?

16:40.210 --> 16:42.760
Um... you're...

16:43.650 --> 16:47.570
<i>If they find out I'm a 
monster, they'll kill me.</i>

16:47.950 --> 16:50.130
It's going to be hard.

16:50.130 --> 16:56.620
No, when I met Isaac, he didn't 
seem to care about my appearance.

16:56.620 --> 16:59.310
If it was an issue, he wouldn't 
have made the request at all.

17:01.230 --> 17:02.680
All right.

17:02.680 --> 17:05.520
But if there's any problem at all, tell me.

17:05.520 --> 17:09.010
Of course. I'll start 
by paying them a visit.

17:11.460 --> 17:15.540
We've come to talk about 
your condition today.

17:17.140 --> 17:20.720
You're sick with Malaccumula.

17:23.160 --> 17:25.560
So it's as I thought.

17:26.270 --> 17:30.020
I'll need to tell the Church 
to send a replacement.

17:32.250 --> 17:34.150
There's no need.

17:35.220 --> 17:36.120
What's this?

17:37.320 --> 17:40.110
A medicine made from Dragonblood flower.

17:41.070 --> 17:43.870
Take one pill a day.

17:43.870 --> 17:48.430
Little by little, it will dissolve 
the foulness building within you.

17:48.730 --> 17:52.430
I appreciate it, but this 
is so expensive, and I...

17:52.430 --> 17:55.760
Headmistress Lilian, you don't 
need to worry about the money!

17:57.120 --> 17:58.660
So please...

17:59.910 --> 18:02.550
Please get better soon!

18:03.470 --> 18:04.840
Alize...

18:05.400 --> 18:09.200
Umberto, don't tell me 
<i>you</i> got this flower...

18:09.200 --> 18:13.780
I did used to be an adventurer, but 
somebody like me could never do that.

18:13.780 --> 18:18.940
An adventurer took the job from Alize, 
for the price of one bronze piece.

18:22.180 --> 18:23.540
I see...

18:24.120 --> 18:26.820
It was the one who came 
here that day, wasn't it?

18:44.350 --> 18:47.710
Excuse me... is Isaac in?

18:47.710 --> 18:50.820
Yes. He's in the mansion.

18:50.820 --> 18:53.340
Please, go inside.

18:53.340 --> 18:55.400
It looks like there's a maze...

18:55.400 --> 18:58.120
Yes. Be careful.

18:58.790 --> 19:02.210
Even if I was told to come here for a job?

19:02.840 --> 19:04.090
Yes.

19:06.770 --> 19:08.580
Do maps cost money?

19:08.580 --> 19:11.150
There'd be no point in having one.

19:12.230 --> 19:16.090
A special magic item was 
used to make this garden.

19:16.090 --> 19:18.470
The path changes.

19:18.470 --> 19:20.900
There's an item that can do that?

19:20.900 --> 19:23.800
No... even if it exists, that's incredible!

19:24.190 --> 19:28.790
The heads of the Latour family have 
always collected magic items.

19:28.790 --> 19:33.060
I'm told that this item was 
a part of their collection.

19:33.760 --> 19:38.230
I don't like the fact that I have to 
make it past one of their hobbies.

19:38.230 --> 19:41.010
Even if I told you there's a reward?

19:41.010 --> 19:42.150
A reward?

19:43.300 --> 19:47.050
Those who make it through the 
maze and reach the mansion

19:47.050 --> 19:50.650
can receive a magic item from 
the head of the household.

19:50.650 --> 19:51.920
Really?

19:52.660 --> 19:57.330
The entrance to the maze is only opened 
rarely, at the whim of the head of household.

19:57.840 --> 20:00.390
I'm sure that's the case today.

20:01.300 --> 20:03.600
Thanks for telling me.

20:03.600 --> 20:05.730
One more thing...

20:05.730 --> 20:09.230
I'd like to ask something from someone who 
I assume has completed the maze himself.

20:09.230 --> 20:10.130
Yes?

20:10.870 --> 20:13.030
Any advice?

20:13.810 --> 20:15.620
Hmm...

20:16.280 --> 20:20.690
The sun won't help you. I suppose 
that's enough of a hint.

20:23.110 --> 20:24.330
The sun?

20:27.490 --> 20:28.610
Thank you.

20:35.190 --> 20:37.380
<i>They're giving me a magic item.</i>

20:37.380 --> 20:39.630
<i>Of course I'm going to try it.</i>

20:42.540 --> 20:45.310
<i>Even this cursed mask is a magic item...</i>

20:45.310 --> 20:47.530
<i>And it wouldn't be cheap 
if I bought it normally.</i>

20:47.960 --> 20:51.510
<i>If I can get a powerful magic item...</i>

20:52.150 --> 20:56.190
<i>I need money and equipment if I'm 
going to become Mythril-class, too!</i>

21:25.420 --> 21:26.700
<i>No luck, huh?</i>

21:27.120 --> 21:32.070
<i>Even if a magic item made this place, it's 
not a Labyrinth so it won't work, perhaps.</i>

21:32.620 --> 21:36.080
<i>That's fine. I've got a 
good sense of direction.</i>

21:36.810 --> 21:40.770
<i>I can draw a mental map that's more 
than enough for a maze of this size...</i>

